--- body ---
## Context

The library-level bench (ticket 0719, merged in PR #406) put 100 questions
from the author's own library to the reviewed zoteus build and found
cross-lingual retrieval near zero, in every retrieval mode:

| lane | n | win | near-win | miss |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| en→en | 59 | 20 | 35 | 4 |
| vi→vi | 8 | 1 | 5 | 2 |
| fr→en | 12 | 1 | 4 | 7 |
| vi→en | 10 | 0 | 0 | 10 |

Keyword found the work in 3 of 30 cross-lingual cases, vectors in 9, hybrid
in 9, so the failure is not a mode effect. Same-language retrieval is healthy
at 0,76 reciprocal rank for English.

**What the run did not record is which model produced those vectors.** The
run identity says the embedder is local and active; it does not name it. That
single fact decides what the finding means, and the two readings are opposite:

- If the build loaded a **multilingual** embedder, this is a failure of a
  requirement the project has ratified, and R29 is broken at library level in
  the direction ruling 2 of 2026-09-06 added, a Vietnamese query against
  English content.
- If the build loaded the **English-only incumbent** (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, the
  model the feasibility runs used), then the numbers are the expected
  behaviour of a monolingual model and say nothing about R29. What they would
  then be evidence for is a shipped default that cannot keep R7 or R29 at all.

Reporting either reading before the model is named would be a verdict dressed
as a finding (`rules/workflow.md` § Diagnosis discipline).

## Actions

1. Read, from the reviewed build's own source and configuration rather than
   from documentation, which model the default path loads: the registry entry,
   the resolved model id, its dtype and pooling.
2. Record the model id, revision and pooling in the bench's `run` block, so no
   future run can be read without it. SPEC.md §5.2.10 already requires a run
   identity; this is the field it is missing.
3. Re-run the cross-lingual lanes and state the verdict against R29 explicitly,
   naming the model.
4. If the default is monolingual, say so where a reader of the requirement
   will meet it, and open the question of what the shipped default should be.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] the embedder actually loaded by the default path is named, from source
- [ ] the bench's run identity carries model id, revision, dtype and pooling
- [ ] the cross-lingual lanes re-run and their verdict against R29 stated with
      the model named
